ed speaking french and  that revolutionized my french because i  started using it every single day so it  doesn't have to be love it can be  friendship it can be traveling it can be  using a language family it can be  anything but it's important to  find that one perspective that one  activity or those activities because  those are the ones that in the long run  are going to cause you to speak the  language fluently because it takes time  takes experiences i like thinking of  language learning as a timeline and as a  story that you build for yourself every  for every language you learn you have as  another story  and you have another storyline and you  have a new identity that you build on  top of the one you already have and this  is this is very important if you want to  speak a language really well okay guys  so in this video we've talked about the  five things that polygons do differently  and that allow them to learn a bunch of  languages successfully but we have also  made another video about another very  important thing and that is mindset how  polyglots think about themselves and  about the process of language learning  makes a huge difference and we have made  this video that you can watch by  clicking here somewhere on the video and  that is on gabriel's channel so check  that out because it's a very interesting  video so  that's it for now bye from me luca and  bye from  gabriel thanks and see you in the other  video bye  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

